# Cursor Rules — AI-Powered Bar Management System

## Context
Bar management system for Thai counter bars. NestJS backend + Next.js frontend. Senior project, production-grade quality expected.
Full context: CLAUDE.md | Features: docs/FRD.md | Schema: docs/schema.sql | Session state: docs/handoff.md

## Code Style

### General
- TypeScript strict mode. No `any` — use `unknown` and narrow it.
- Prefer explicit return types on all functions.
- Named exports over default exports (except Next.js pages/layouts).
- No barrel files (`index.ts` re-exports) in backend modules — they cause circular dependency issues with NestJS DI.

### NestJS (backend/)
- Layer order: controller → service → repository. No business logic in controllers.
- One module per domain. Module boundaries follow ERD domains.
- Always use `PermissionsGuard` — never inline permission checks.
- Use `save()` not `update()` on TypeORM entities (AuditSubscriber requires it).
- DTOs with `class-validator` on all controller inputs. Whitelist enabled globally.
- Async/await throughout. No `.then()` chains.
- Use `@nestjs/cls` for request-scoped context (current user for audit).

### Next.js (frontend/)
- App Router. Server Components by default; `'use client'` only when needed.
- Tailwind CSS only — no inline styles, no CSS modules.
- Import alias `@/*` maps to `./src/*`.
- Fetch data in Server Components or React Query (client). No direct API calls inside event handlers.

## Architecture Rules
- No microservices. One NestJS process (REST + WebSocket + webhook).
- No Prisma — TypeORM only (Prisma requires build-time network for binary download on ECS).
- No Redux — React Query for server state, Zustand if client state needed.
- Redis does 4 jobs: ACL cache, session, BullMQ queue, WebSocket pub/sub. Don't add a 5th unless discussed.
- BullMQ for async jobs — webhook response must return 200 fast, enqueue and process async.

## What NOT to do
- Do not split backend into separate services or containers.
- Do not use `update()` on audited TypeORM entities.
- Do not add offline mode, member QR, or staff performance analytics (cut from scope).
- Do not touch audit_log with UPDATE/DELETE — append only.
- Do not add Kubernetes/EKS until ECS is stable.
- Do not expand scope without a deliberate decision — finish order → pay → close first.
